[h1]Probably Stolen Workshop Uploader[/h1]
A Workshop uploader built into the game, so you can publish or update your tested mods without ever leaving the shop.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ How to Use[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Opening it:[/b] Press [b]F9[/b] to force it open or closed. A Workshop Uploader entry is added to the in-game [b]Mods[/b] settings, where you can create a new Workshop item, or search for and link an existing one.
[*][b]What it does:[/b] Using the Steam account you launched the game with, it creates Workshop items and updates existing ones for you — uploading the files, description, images and mod tags. A built-in BBCode editor supports drafts, templates and live preview. Once the upload finishes, you can jump straight to the Workshop page to check the result.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Multi-language[/h2]

[list]
[*]Titles and descriptions are [b]stored per language[/b]: English, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Japanese, Korean, French, German, Spanish and Russian.
[*]Submit again after switching language to update that language's title and description on the Workshop; other language versions stay untouched.
[*]Switching language never discards what you've typed — you can go back and forth freely.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]◆ Notes[/h2]

[list]
[*]This project is adapted from the STS2 Workshop Uploader. Original project: [url=https://github.com/BAKAOLC/STS2-WorkshopUploaderMod]https://github.com/BAKAOLC/STS2-WorkshopUploaderMod[/url]
[*]The UI occasionally freezes — press [b]F9[/b] to refresh. F9 is the force toggle for this window; it also works during gameplay, though using it mid-run isn't recommended.
[*]Found a serious bug? Report it in the comments and I'll drop back in to fix it while I'm busy with Phantom Blade Zero.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[i](Phantom Blade Zero just released, so Probably Stolen is on the back burner for now — updates will be slower, but comments are still read.)[/i]
